WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.210
Speaker 1: The Georgia Senate runoff has gone
completely off the rails as Republican Senate

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:15.519
candidate Herschel Walker has accused Rafal
Warnock of sexual assault and physical assault.

00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:16.789
What?

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:18.620
What is he talking about?

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:19.640
None of us know.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.109
And increasingly the question is being asked.

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:25.860
Does Walker even have any idea what he's talking
about?

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.220
Is this defamation?

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.289
Let's look at the clip.

00:00:28.289 --> 00:00:31.380
This is you know, to say it's gotten ugly
is an understatement.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:36.410
I genuinely don't know whether Walker has
any idea what he's saying, but that would

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.010
not be an excuse here.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.670
That would not be an excuse.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:44.469
This is the height of dangerous irresponsibility.

00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:47.949
Herschel Walker spoke yesterday at some event.

00:00:47.949 --> 00:00:50.120
He's doing these campaign events all over
Georgia.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:55.730
And he said, you know, there was physical
abuse and there was sexual abuse.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.260
Who did it?

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.190
It has to be Senator Raphael Warnock.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:03.069
Now, I'll tell you what this relates to in
a moment.

00:01:03.069 --> 00:01:04.069
Here's the clip.

00:01:04.069 --> 00:01:05.069
Speaker 2: He's not what do you think it's
going to be?

00:01:05.069 --> 00:01:06.069
It's only the best people that know him best.

00:01:06.069 --> 00:01:07.069
Say that he's an actor.

00:01:07.069 --> 00:01:08.069
He's an actor.

00:01:08.069 --> 00:01:10.280
I don't know what he did at that camp as well.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.240
Y'all may not have heard this.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:15.980
This young man said it was a sexual abuse.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:17.150
That was physical abuse.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:18.330
Somebody who did that.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:24.000
It had to be Senator Raphael Warnock because
he's responsible for it.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.000
You ought to hear about that.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.360
Did you he don't want to talk about those
things because he don't want you to know that

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.880
he think you're going to be he gets a good
senator for you.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.630
I'll tell you right now, it is time for a
change.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:34.620
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:43.700
Now, if you can make heads or tails out of
that unintelligible word salad, by all means,

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.930
go ahead and do it.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:54.790
This is so difficult because Walker clearly
is saying that Raphael Warnock sexually abused

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:57.860
and physically abused a kid.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:03.860
It's clear that he's saying those words, but
at the same time, it's never really clear

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:06.899
that Walker has any idea what he's saying.

00:02:06.899 --> 00:02:09.750
And I know every time we talk about this oh,
David.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:15.420
Well, that's not really issues oriented or
he has a brain injury from football that hasn't

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:20.310
been said, or this is because of his dissociative
identity disorder that he says these things.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:23.060
That's not the explanation that they're giving.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:25.950
We have to go by what he is saying.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.629
And there's a real question as to whether
this is potentially defamatory.

00:02:29.629 --> 00:02:36.239
Now, again, it's not clear Walker knows what
he's saying because it's never clear he knows

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:37.239
what he's saying.

00:02:37.239 --> 00:02:46.879
But what this is about relates to allegations
that camp counselors 20 years ago at a camp

00:02:46.879 --> 00:02:50.330
were Warnock.

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:54.099
Warnock ran the camp, but there's no allegations
that Warnock did any of this stuff.

00:02:54.099 --> 00:03:00.569
The allegation is that a 12 year old boy was
forced to sleep outside at the camp and had

00:03:00.569 --> 00:03:03.989
urine tossed on him by camp counselors.

00:03:03.989 --> 00:03:05.290
Okay.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:08.270
Absolutely horrible allegations.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:12.740
And the incident was investigated in 2000
122.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.629
It resulted in no charges.

00:03:14.629 --> 00:03:20.980
Law enforcement later called it a miscommunication
and it was never even alleged that Warnock

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.200
did any of this stuff.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:27.290
Now, you could say, well, if indeed it happened,
maybe Raphael Warnock, who was running the

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.230
camp, had some ultimate responsibility.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:36.310
But the idea that Warnock is a sexual or physical
abuser is completely out of this world.

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:39.659
Now the question then becomes, is this defamatory?

00:03:39.659 --> 00:03:44.010
Because in general, you know, if some random
person on Twitter with five followers tweets

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:48.220
that Raphael Warnock sexually and physically
abused someone.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:52.370
It's not defamatory because it's not damaging
to Warnock.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:58.760
But when we look at the requirements for defamation,
the information that is allegedly defamatory

00:03:58.760 --> 00:03:59.850
must be published.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:01.420
Well, that means that it's public.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.420
And here is the video.

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:03.420
We looked at the video.

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.150
So it certainly meets that standard.

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:09.069
The person being defamed was clearly identified
by the statement.

00:04:09.069 --> 00:04:13.480
Meaning is it clear that Walker is talking
about his opponent?

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:16.959
Senator Raphael Warnock I would argue it's
clear that that is, he says.

00:04:16.959 --> 00:04:18.579
Raphael Warnock is the one who did this.

00:04:18.579 --> 00:04:22.520
There's no confusion as to whether he means
someone else by that name or anything like

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:23.520
that.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.900
Number three, the remarks have a negative
effect on the person's reputation.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:28.389
That's the question.

00:04:28.389 --> 00:04:29.620
We don't know yet.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:36.810
But if it starts to spread in such a tight
race, the completely baseless allegation that

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:40.860
Warnock is a physical and sexual abuse, or
you could argue that those remarks have a

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:44.090
negative impact on Warnock's reputation.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:47.710
Number four is, is the information demonstrably
false?

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:52.450
Well, it's hard to prove negatives, but there's
certainly no evidence that these allegations

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:54.150
about Warnock are true.

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:58.250
And the police investigation generally into
this incident at the camp, which isn't even

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:05.100
alleged to be warnock's doing found no legal
wrongdoing, and it didn't even allege that

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.300
Warnock was the one doing it.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.450
And then number five, the defendant is at
fault.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:14.800
In other words, that it is indeed Herschel
Walker, who made made these claims and made

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:21.390
them in a way that is consistent with with
reckless disregard or there's different different

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:23.310
standards in different states.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:26.250
You arguably have a defamation case here.

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:33.259
Now, what I care more about is can we just
get Raphael Warnock over the finish line before

00:05:33.259 --> 00:05:37.190
some new thing comes up that gets in the way
of this campaign?

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:43.069
And I think, again, without defending or attacking
the individual incident and what supposedly

00:05:43.069 --> 00:05:48.910
happened to this 12 year old, what Walker
said is not even remotely based, in fact,

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.410
than the crowd just sort of goes along with
it.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:57.069
The real disturbing part of all of this is
that this race even went to a runoff.

00:05:57.069 --> 00:06:01.639
That's really the disturbing part that the
Georgia voters, Georgia Republican voters,

00:06:01.639 --> 00:06:08.590
and this is a theme that we are following
in their desperation to not vote for a Democrat.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:14.479
They are voting for someone who is completely
unqualified, doesn't have a sensible position

00:06:14.479 --> 00:06:22.120
that he can articulate on any issue and on
a personal level is a complete hypocrite with

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:26.410
regard to the policy positions that he sort
of claims to advocate to the extent that we

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:30.729
can understand him completely against abortion,
in all cases, no exception.

00:06:30.729 --> 00:06:35.890
Well, he urged two women and paid for two
women to get abortions.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:40.139
Says we need we need men not to be absent
fathers.

00:06:40.139 --> 00:06:43.240
He's an absent father to multiple kids that
we know about.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:47.610
It's not even totally clear to me how many
kids it is, and on and on and on.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:51.040
That alone is not a reason to vote against
him.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:55.349
But the totality of the situation should lead
to this guy losing by 40 points.

00:06:55.349 --> 00:06:59.740
And instead it was so close within one point,
with neither candidate able to secure 50%

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:03.569
of the vote that now we have a runoff on December
6th.

00:07:03.569 --> 00:07:09.240
Let's really hope that our Georgia friends
who vote in Georgia get out there and make

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.260
this extraordinarily important vote.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.330
We'll have live coverage on December six.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:15.289
That's the day of the runoff

